{
  "kanji": "響",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 響\ntitle: resound; echo\njlpt: 1\ntags: [jlpt-n1, grade-8, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 20\nradical: 音\nradicalNumber: 180\nonyomi: [キョウ]\nkunyomi: [ひび.く]\nquizOnyomi: [キョウ]\nquizKunyomi: [ひび.く]\ndistractors: [境, 競, 鏡]\nquiz_exclusions: [音, 鳴, 声, 震, 効]\n---\n\n# 響 — resound; echo\n\n**Strokes:** 20 · **Key (radical):** 音 (no. 180), at the bottom · **JLPT:** N1 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n響 concerns sound resounding or carrying, and extends to an effect reaching\nsomething else. [響く](../words/響く.md) ひびく can describe a sound\nechoing or an event affecting something; [響き](../words/響き.md)\nひびき is a sound, resonance or impression in the relevant context.\n\n[影響](../words/影響.md) えいきょう means influence or effect.\nIt need not concern any audible sound. Do not restrict the character to\nliteral echoes merely because that is the easiest image to remember.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** find 郷 above [音](音.md).\nImagine a sound rising from the lower 音 and reaching every corner of the\nintricate upper block. This is a visual memory aid, not a verified historical\nor sound-component analysis. 郷 has no kanji card here yet.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| キョウ | on | [影響](../words/影響.md) えいきょう - influence; effect |\n| ひび.く | kun | [響く](../words/響く.md) ひびく - resound; affect |\n\nBoth readings are selected with linked examples. 響く is an intransitive\ngodan verb: 響 writes ひび and く is written in kana.\nThe noun 響き ひびき is related, but its final き is part of that noun's\nspelling, not a replacement ending to insert into every use of 響く.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [響く](../words/響く.md) ひびく - resound; have an effect\n- [響き](../words/響き.md) ひびき - sound; resonance; impression\n- [影響](../words/影響.md) えいきょう - influence; effect\n\n## Notes\n\n- [境](境.md), boundary, [競](競.md), compete, and [鏡](鏡.md),\n  mirror, have related upright shapes and readings, but different complete\n  forms and meanings. 響 has 音 at the bottom, not the lower shapes of those cards.\n- Sounding overlaps [音](音.md), [鳴](鳴.md) and [声](声.md);\n  vibration overlaps [震](震.md), and effect overlaps [効](効.md).\n  They are useful semantic comparisons, not clearly wrong meaning choices.\n- JMdict separately records 響く どよめく and 響き どよめき in other\n  lexical entries, with kana-preferred or rare-kanji qualifications.\n  Those are not free alternate readings for the linked ひびく and ひびき\n  examples. Bare 響 for ひびき is itself an irregular-okurigana spelling;\n  use the full spelling 響き shown here.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project),\n2026-11-02 snapshot. Complete word families and spelling qualifications:\n[JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project),\nentries 1173660, 1602130, 1009280, 1238610 and 1612890.\nCharacter senses: [Digital Daijisen, 響](https://www.weblio.jp/content/響).\nStandard readings: [Official Joyo table, PDF p. 39](https://www.bunka.go.jp/kokugo_nihongo/sisaku/joho/joho/kijun/naikaku/pdf/joyokanjihyo_20101130.pdf#page=39).\n",
